<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2TH" style="id">2 THESSALONIANS</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2TH 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Apostolic Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 1:1"/>
    Paul and Silvanus and Timothy,
    <verse eid="2TH 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 1:2"/>
    Grace to you, and peace from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ. 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Giving Thanks to God on Behalf of the Saints</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 1:3"/>
    We ought always to give thanks to God concerning you, brothers, just as it is fitting, because your faith is growing greatly and the love of each and every one of you toward another is increasing, 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:3"/>
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 1:4"/>
    so that we ourselves boast about you among the churches of God for your perseverance and faith in all your persecutions and in the afflictions which you are enduring.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Eschatological Judgment and Glory</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 1:5"/>
    This is an indication of the righteous judgment of God, so that you may be considered worthy of the kingdom of God, for which you are also suffering. 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:5"/>
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 1:6"/>
    For indeed, it is just with God to repay those who are afflicting you with affliction, 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:6"/>
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 1:7"/>
    and to you who are being afflicted, rest with us at the revelation of the Lord Jesus from heaven with His mighty angels 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:7"/>
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 1:8"/>
    in blazing flame, inflicting just punishment on those who do not know God, and who do not obey the gospel of our Lord Jesus.* 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:8"/>
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 1:9"/>
    These* will pay the penalty of eternal destruction, away from the presence of the Lord and from the glory of his strength, 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:9"/>
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 1:10"/>
    when He comes to be glorified in His saints on that day and to be marveled at among all those who have believed, because our testimony to you was believed. 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 1:11"/>
    For this* purpose also, we pray always for you, that our God may count you worthy of His calling, and bring to completion your every desire for goodness and your every faith-driven work by His power,* 
    <verse eid="2TH 1:11"/>
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 1:12"/>
    so that the name of our Lord Jesus may be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">
    8 Some ancient manuscripts omit the name 
    <char style="it">Jesus</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    9 Greek 
    <char style="it">who</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    11 Greek 
    <char style="it">which</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    11 Greek 
    <char style="it">…and bring to completion every desire for goodness and work of faith by power</char>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2TH 2"/>
  <para style="s1">The Revelation of the Man of Lawlessness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 2:1"/>
    Now we ask you, brothers, concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our gathering together to Him, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:1"/>
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 2:2"/>
    that you not be quickly shaken from your composure nor be alarmed, either by a spirit, or a spoken* word, or a written correspondence purported to be from us,* claiming that* the day of the Lord has arrived. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:2"/>
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 2:3"/>
    Do not let anyone deceive you in any way, because that day will not come* unless the apostasy comes first and the man of lawlessness is revealed, the son of destruction, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:3"/>
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 2:4"/>
    the one who opposes and exalts himself over every so-called god or object of worship, so that he takes his seat in the temple of God, presenting himself as God. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 2:5"/>
    Do you not remember that while I was still with you, I was saying these things to you? 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:5"/>
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 2:6"/>
    And you know that which is restraining him now, so that he might be revealed in his own time. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:6"/>
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 2:7"/>
    For the mystery of lawlessness is at work already; only the One who now restrains will do so* until He is taken out of the way. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:7"/>
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 2:8"/>
    And then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord Jesus* will eliminate with the breath of His mouth, and bring to nothing by the appearance of His coming, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:8"/>
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 2:9"/>
    whose arrival corresponds with the working of Satan with all power and signs and false wonders, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:9"/>
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 2:10"/>
    and with every deception of unrighteousness for those who are perishing, because they did not accept the love of the truth, so that they would be saved. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:10"/>
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 2:11"/>
    And for this reason, God sends them a delusion-causing power,** so that they will believe the lie, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:11"/>
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 2:12"/>
    in order that all may be judged who did not believe the truth, but delighted in unrighteousness. 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Giving Thanks to God</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 2:13"/>
    But we ought to give thanks to God always concerning you, brothers beloved by the Lord, because God has chosen you from the beginning for salvation through sanctification by the Spirit and belief in the truth, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:13"/>
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 2:14"/>
    for which purpose He called you through our gospel, for obtaining the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Encouragement to Stand Resolute</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 2:15"/>
    So then, brothers, stand resolute and firmly uphold the traditions which you were taught, whether by spoken word or by written correspondence from us.
    <verse eid="2TH 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 2:16"/>
    Now may our Lord Jesus Christ Himself and God our Father, the One who loved us and gave us eternal comfort and good hope through grace, 
    <verse eid="2TH 2:16"/>
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 2:17"/>
    encourage and strengthen your hearts in every good work and word.*
    <verse eid="2TH 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">
    2 The verb 
    <char style="it">spoken</char>
     is contextually supplied for clarity. So also v. 15
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    2 Greek 
    <char style="it">as if from us</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    2 Greek 
    <char style="it">as though the</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    3 The negative future independent clause 
    <char style="it">that day will not come</char>
     is contextually supplied for clarity
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    7 The verb phrase pro-form 
    <char style="it">will do so </char>
    is contextually supplied for clarity
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    8 Some ancient manuscripts omit the name 
    <char style="it">Jesus</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    11 Greek 
    <char style="it">a power of delusion/error</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    11 Or 
    <char style="it">an error-causing power</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    17 Some ancient manuscripts read 
    <char style="it">in every good word and work</char>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2TH 3"/>
  <para style="s1">Paul's Appeal for Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2TH 3:1"/>
    Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may advance speedily and be glorified, just as it was also with you, 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:1"/>
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2TH 3:2"/>
    and that we may be delivered from improper* and evil men,* for not all have faith. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:2"/>
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2TH 3:3"/>
    But the Lord is faithful, who will strengthen you and guard you against the evil one. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:3"/>
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2TH 3:4"/>
    And we have confidence in the Lord concerning you, that you are doing and will do the things which we are commanding.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2TH 3:5"/>
    Now may the Lord direct your hearts into the love of God and into the perseverance of Christ. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Warning Against Idleness</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2TH 3:6"/>
    And we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that you keep away from every brother who walks disorderly and not according to the tradition which they received from us. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:6"/>
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2TH 3:7"/>
    For you yourselves know how you ought to imitate us, that we did not behave disorderly among you, 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:7"/>
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2TH 3:8"/>
    nor did we eat bread from anyone freely, but with labor and toil, working night and day so as not to burden any of you. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:8"/>
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2TH 3:9"/>
    It was* not that we do not have the right, but that we might offer ourselves as an example for you, so that you would imitate us. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:9"/>
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2TH 3:10"/>
    For even when we were with you, we consistently issued this command, that if anyone is not willing to work, then he should not eat, either. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:10"/>
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2TH 3:11"/>
    For we hear that some among you are walking disorderly, not working at all, but being busybodies. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:11"/>
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2TH 3:12"/>
    Now such individuals we command and exhort in the Lord Jesus Christ* that, working with quietness, they may eat their own bread.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2TH 3:13"/>
    But you, brothers, do not grow weary in doing what is right. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:13"/>
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2TH 3:14"/>
    But if anyone does not obey our message in this letter, mark this person, and do not associate with him, so that he may be put to shame. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:14"/>
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2TH 3:15"/>
    Yet do not regard him as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Pauline Prayer</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2TH 3:16"/>
    Now may the Lord of peace Himself grant you peace continually* in every way. The Lord be with all of you.
    <verse eid="2TH 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2TH 3:17"/>
    I, Paul, write this greeting in my own hand—which is a mark of authenticity in every letter. This is the way I write. 
    <verse eid="2TH 3:17"/>
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2TH 3:18"/>
    The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with all of you.*
    <verse eid="2TH 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">
    2 Or 
    <char style="it">perverse</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    2 Or 
    <char style="it">people, </char>
    as the term is understood generically speaking
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    9 The dummy/expletive subject construction 
    <char style="it">It was </char>
    is supplied to the text based on context for the sake of clarity
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    12 Some ancient manuscripts read 
    <char style="it">through our Lord Jesus Christ</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    16 Greek 
    <char style="it">through all</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    17 Greek 
    <char style="it">The greeting is in/by my own hand—Paul’s</char>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    18 Some ancient manuscripts insert 
    <char style="it">Amen </char>
    at this point
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2TH 3"/>
</usx>
